crypto-ffi: expose the identity-based sharing strategy and is_cross_signed_by_owner

Kotlin callers of matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi can only pick AllDevices,
OnlyTrustedDevices or ErrorOnVerifiedUserProblem today. The identity-based
strategy (share only with devices signed by their owner's cross-signing
identity) is what keeps a device injected by a compromised server from
receiving room keys without asking users to verify each contact; the WASM
bindings already expose it as CollectStrategy.identityBasedStrategy().

- EncryptionSettings.identity_based_strategy (default false, so existing
  Kotlin callers are unchanged).
- Device.is_cross_signed_by_owner.

Against tag matrix-sdk-crypto-0.19.1 (commit b18166c68bb958a21f0bca8b2d8320cb53583362).
Not compiled locally (no Rust toolchain on the workstation): the build workflow
is the first compilation. To be proposed upstream as is (D-238).

